// Declarations about the document itself: `::name`, on lines at the top.
//
// They are not content. A `::` that opens no line is text, so `std::vec` and
// a `::kind(x)` in the middle of a sentence below are prose.

::kind(note)
::id(doc-sample)
::meta{ title: "A note with a preamble" }

=[ Declarations ]

Rust writes std::vec and mem::swap(a, b); a ::kind(x) in the middle of a line
is only text.

```tmt
::kind(config)
```

A declaration stays out of the output.
